WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:02.868
-Welcome, welcome, welcome to
"The Tonight Show"!

00:00:02.868 --> 00:00:04.234
You're here. You made it.

00:00:04.234 --> 00:00:06.634
You're watching.
Thank you very much.

00:00:06.634 --> 00:00:08.300
Well, guys, this is big.

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:11.033
Last night the January 6th
commission revealed that

00:00:11.033 --> 00:00:13.834
during the Capitol riots,
the White House Chief of Staff

00:00:13.834 --> 00:00:16.901
got texts pleading for Trump to
calm things down

00:00:16.901 --> 00:00:20.067
from Fox News anchors
and Donald Trump Jr.

00:00:20.067 --> 00:00:21.734
[ Audience murmurs ]
Yeah.

00:00:21.734 --> 00:00:25.801
Trump ignored the advice of the
closest to him and also Don Jr.

00:00:25.801 --> 00:00:27.634
[ Laughter ]

00:00:27.634 --> 00:00:30.033
Trump was like, "If I replied to
every text that said

00:00:30.033 --> 00:00:32.200
'What you're doing is crazy,'
I'd never get anything done."

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:33.934
[ Laughter ]

00:00:33.934 --> 00:00:35.467
Yeah, it came out
that Fox News hosts

00:00:35.467 --> 00:00:37.000
were begging Trump
to do something.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:39.701
And today, Fox News hosts
lit their tree on fire again

00:00:39.701 --> 00:00:42.267
just to change the subject.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:42.267 --> 00:00:44.901
[ Applause ]

00:00:44.901 --> 00:00:46.467
Trump didn't want to hear it.

00:00:46.467 --> 00:00:48.534
Not only did he ignore the texts
from Fox News,

00:00:48.534 --> 00:00:51.067
he also dropped them from
his family cellphone plan.

00:00:51.067 --> 00:00:52.667
[ Laughter ]

00:00:52.667 --> 00:00:55.133
That's right, White House
Chief of Staff Mark Meadows was

00:00:55.133 --> 00:00:58.100
getting texts during the attack
asking Trump to intervene.

00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:01.100
For example, Sean Hannity
texted -- and this is real --

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:04.534
"Can he make a statement, ask
people to leave the Capitol?"

00:01:04.534 --> 00:01:06.601
Yep, that's not all Meadows
received.

00:01:06.601 --> 00:01:08.167
Several other messages that day
too.

00:01:08.167 --> 00:01:09.868
For example, Eric Trump texted,

00:01:09.868 --> 00:01:11.934
"Head stuck in Capitol
staircase railing.

00:01:11.934 --> 00:01:13.033
Send help!"

00:01:13.033 --> 00:01:16.133
[ Laughter ]

00:01:16.133 --> 00:01:18.067
Next up, Rudy Gillian texted,

00:01:18.067 --> 00:01:20.501
"Just showed up
at Capitol Total Landscaping.

00:01:20.501 --> 00:01:21.968
When's the riotin' start?"

00:01:21.968 --> 00:01:23.834
[ Laughter ]

00:01:23.834 --> 00:01:26.067
And finally President Trump
texted Meadows,

00:01:26.067 --> 00:01:27.968
"Just make sure they don't take
away my Twitter!"

00:01:27.968 --> 00:01:29.167
Yeah, there you go.
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:29.167 --> 00:01:31.834
Crazy day all around.
Crazy day all around.

00:01:31.834 --> 00:01:35.100
[ Applause ]

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:36.667
Some more news from Washington.

00:01:36.667 --> 00:01:38.501
The White House just announced
their plan to add

00:01:38.501 --> 00:01:40.868
500,000 charging stations

00:01:40.868 --> 00:01:43.033
for electric vehicles
across the country.

00:01:43.033 --> 00:01:44.601
It's incredible.

00:01:44.601 --> 00:01:46.901
Somehow we can build half
a million charging stations,

00:01:46.901 --> 00:01:49.267
but we can't add a second outlet
at LaGuardia.

00:01:49.267 --> 00:01:50.868
[ Laughter ]

00:01:50.868 --> 00:01:53.801
Can I charge my phone?
I just -- Okay.

00:01:53.801 --> 00:01:55.234
You guys hear this?

00:01:55.234 --> 00:01:57.934
Today, the State of New York
ordered former governor

00:01:57.934 --> 00:02:01.634
Andrew Cuomo to return
the $5 million he received from

00:02:01.634 --> 00:02:04.234
his book on leadership
during the pandemic.

00:02:04.234 --> 00:02:06.334
I think it's safe
to say the drinking

00:02:06.334 --> 00:02:08.534
at the Cuomo family
Christmas has already begun.

00:02:08.534 --> 00:02:10.300
[ Laughter ]

00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:12.834
Some business news -- After
announcing their name change,

00:02:12.834 --> 00:02:15.167
Facebook paid a bank
in South Dakota

00:02:15.167 --> 00:02:19.634
$60 million for the
rights to their new name, Meta.

00:02:19.634 --> 00:02:23.067
It's making me emotional because
seeing a bank get $60 million

00:02:23.067 --> 00:02:24.534
is what Christmas is all about.

00:02:24.534 --> 00:02:26.667
[ Laughter ]

00:02:26.667 --> 00:02:33.033
[ Applause ]

00:02:33.033 --> 00:02:34.801
That's right, a bank.

00:02:34.801 --> 00:02:36.467
Now they're so rich,
they don't even chain

00:02:36.467 --> 00:02:38.367
their pens to the table anymore.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:38.367 --> 00:02:40.467
"Just take them!
That's a Montblanc.

00:02:40.467 --> 00:02:42.834
Just take it."

00:02:42.834 --> 00:02:44.834
I like how Facebook
was trying to rename

00:02:44.834 --> 00:02:46.968
their company something "cool,"
but it was already being used

00:02:46.968 --> 00:02:48.467
by a bank in South Dakota.

00:02:48.467 --> 00:02:50.067
[ Laughter ]

00:02:50.067 --> 00:02:51.601
Well, this is encouraging.

00:02:51.601 --> 00:02:53.868
I read that despite
supply chain issues,

00:02:53.868 --> 00:02:57.467
UPS and the Postal Service
have improved their on-time

00:02:57.467 --> 00:03:00.234
deliveries compared to
last year's holiday season.

00:03:00.234 --> 00:03:01.400
That's right.

00:03:01.400 --> 00:03:02.901
They now deliver
that little slip that says,

00:03:02.901 --> 00:03:04.667
"Sorry we missed you"
right on time.

00:03:04.667 --> 00:03:07.300
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:07.300 --> 00:03:11.167
Right on time.
"Ah, I was here all day."

00:03:11.167 --> 00:03:15.567
I saw that LG has a new
battery-powered TV that you can

00:03:15.567 --> 00:03:18.234
wheel around on a stand
to watch anywhere.

00:03:18.234 --> 00:03:20.434
Yeah, a TV on wheels.

00:03:20.434 --> 00:03:22.234
It is perfect
if you've ever dreamt of being

00:03:22.234 --> 00:03:24.567
a substitute teacher from 1997.

00:03:24.567 --> 00:03:28.167
[ Laughter ]

00:03:28.167 --> 00:03:31.367
And get this -- Uber Eats just
made its first-ever delivery

00:03:31.367 --> 00:03:35.267
to space after a Japanese
billionaire brought food

00:03:35.267 --> 00:03:38.934
from the app to astronauts on
the International Space Station.

00:03:38.934 --> 00:03:40.634
That's how tough the economy is
right now --

00:03:40.634 --> 00:03:42.434
a billionaire is working for
Uber Eats.

00:03:42.434 --> 00:03:44.133
[ Laughter ]

00:03:44.133 --> 00:03:46.133
Well, this is interesting.
A new study found that

00:03:46.133 --> 00:03:48.100
rocket scientists
and brain surgeons

00:03:48.100 --> 00:03:50.634
are not any smarter
than the general population.

00:03:50.634 --> 00:03:52.234
[ Laughter ]

00:03:52.234 --> 00:03:54.033
That's got to be a great study
to read right before

00:03:54.033 --> 00:03:55.501
you're wheeled in
for brain surgery, right?

00:03:55.501 --> 00:03:57.234
It's like, "Huh?"

00:03:57.234 --> 00:03:59.801
Brain surgeons were like, "You
need to be super smart to know

00:03:59.801 --> 00:04:02.534
about the brain and all those
little tubey things around it."

00:04:02.534 --> 00:04:04.100
[ Laughter ]

00:04:04.100 --> 00:04:06.534
And finally, a woman eating at
a restaurant in New Orleans

00:04:06.534 --> 00:04:09.367
found a dozen pearls in
an oyster that she ordered.

00:04:09.367 --> 00:04:10.501
[ Audience murmurs ]

00:04:10.501 --> 00:04:12.834
The woman said she would
probably sell the pearls

00:04:12.834 --> 00:04:14.934
when they passed in
six to eight hours.

00:04:14.934 --> 00:04:16.934
Guys, we have exactly
four shows left

00:04:16.934 --> 00:04:19.100
before we go on Christmas break,
which means it's time for

00:04:19.100 --> 00:04:20.734
that beloved "Tonight Show"
tradition.

00:04:20.734 --> 00:04:23.834
It's time for "12 Days of
Christmas Sweaters."

00:04:23.834 --> 00:04:25.033
Here we go.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:25.033 --> 00:04:27.434
-♪ 12 days of
Christmas sweaters ♪

00:04:27.434 --> 00:04:31.367
♪ Four days left ♪

00:04:31.367 --> 00:04:32.968
-That's right.

00:04:32.968 --> 00:04:35.734
Every show between now and
Christmas, we'll be giving

00:04:35.734 --> 00:04:39.033
one lucky audience member
a phenomenal Christmas sweater

00:04:39.033 --> 00:04:40.834
from the "Countdown to
Christmas" cabinet.

00:04:40.834 --> 00:04:43.868
Now...
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:43.868 --> 00:04:47.667
Since there are
four shows left --

00:04:47.667 --> 00:04:50.234
wow -- let's open door
number four.

00:04:50.234 --> 00:04:52.534
[ Drum roll ]
Ooh, that's right in the middle.

00:04:52.534 --> 00:04:54.834
Go for it, bud,
whenever you're ready.

00:04:54.834 --> 00:04:56.934
Ah! Very nice.

00:04:56.934 --> 00:04:59.334
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:59.334 --> 00:05:01.100
Beautiful.

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:02.634
Oh!

00:05:02.634 --> 00:05:04.067
Wow. It lights up.

00:05:04.067 --> 00:05:07.067
Can we dim the lights
a little bit?

00:05:07.067 --> 00:05:09.000
I thought it lit up.

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:11.534
Oh, it lights up when you move?

00:05:11.534 --> 00:05:12.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:12.601 --> 00:05:15.000
I don't know what -- Wow.

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:16.334
Oh, yeah.

00:05:16.334 --> 00:05:17.734
Alright. Alright.

00:05:17.734 --> 00:05:19.801
Wow. It just kind of blinks
when it wants to blink.

00:05:19.801 --> 00:05:21.133
Alright, here we go.

00:05:21.133 --> 00:05:23.200
Let's see who's going home with
tonight's sweater, okay?

00:05:23.200 --> 00:05:24.734
Everyone look at
your seat number.

00:05:24.734 --> 00:05:27.534
If I call your number,
come on down.

00:05:27.534 --> 00:05:29.601
Quest, can I get a drum roll,
please?

00:05:29.601 --> 00:05:32.100
[ Drum roll ]

00:05:32.100 --> 00:05:35.133
Seat number 4-3-3!

00:05:35.133 --> 00:05:37.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:37.567 --> 00:05:42.634
♪♪

00:05:42.634 --> 00:05:43.868
Yo!

00:05:43.868 --> 00:05:46.467
♪♪

00:05:46.467 --> 00:05:48.534
Hey!

00:05:48.534 --> 00:05:51.300
Welcome, welcome, welcome.

00:05:51.300 --> 00:05:52.667
Wow.

00:05:52.667 --> 00:05:54.200
Oh, my gosh.

00:05:54.200 --> 00:05:56.167
This is going to be more
like a dress for you.

00:05:56.167 --> 00:05:57.400
[ Laughter ]

00:05:57.400 --> 00:05:58.534
What is your name?

00:05:58.534 --> 00:05:59.834
-I'm Jessica.

00:05:59.834 --> 00:06:01.067
-Jessica, where are you from,
Jessica?

00:06:01.067 --> 00:06:03.167
-Colombia.
-Colombia, oh, my goodness!

00:06:03.167 --> 00:06:06.334
[ Cheers and applause ]
Jessica, welcome to the show.

00:06:06.334 --> 00:06:08.100
-Thank you.
-Thank you for being here.

00:06:08.100 --> 00:06:09.601
Do you have anything like this
at home?

00:06:09.601 --> 00:06:11.000
-No.
-Oh, my gosh.

00:06:11.000 --> 00:06:12.801
Well, would you like to
try it on right now?

00:06:12.801 --> 00:06:15.434
-Well, I feel so happy
to be here,

00:06:15.434 --> 00:06:17.067
especially for this present.

00:06:17.067 --> 00:06:19.934
I was talking with a guy before.

00:06:19.934 --> 00:06:22.534
[ Laughter ]

00:06:22.534 --> 00:06:24.934
They know.
-Is everything okay?

00:06:24.934 --> 00:06:27.200
-The cold weather is crazy
for me here

00:06:27.200 --> 00:06:31.067
because in my country it is
warm, so this is perfect.

00:06:31.067 --> 00:06:32.968
-Try it on.

00:06:32.968 --> 00:06:34.934
I think it'll look great on you.

00:06:34.934 --> 00:06:38.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:38.033 --> 00:06:39.501
Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:06:43.067 --> 00:06:45.367
Yeah. Oh, yeah. Look at this.

00:06:45.367 --> 00:06:46.701
There's no wrong way
to wear it.

00:06:46.701 --> 00:06:48.133
Oh, my good-- Look at this!

00:06:48.133 --> 00:06:50.667
[ Cheers and applause ]
Look at that! Come on now!

00:06:50.667 --> 00:06:51.968
Yes!

00:06:51.968 --> 00:06:53.901
Oh, it's so beautiful.

00:06:53.901 --> 00:06:56.100
Congratulations.
It'll keep you warm.

00:06:56.100 --> 00:06:58.534
Welcome. Thank you for being
here. I appreciate it.

00:06:58.534 --> 00:07:00.534
One more time for our audience
member right there.

00:07:00.534 --> 00:07:01.667
Stick around.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:01.667 --> 00:07:03.734
When we come back,
we're singing

00:07:03.734 --> 00:07:06.634
a special Christmas song
with Matthew McConaughey!

00:07:06.634 --> 00:07:07.734
Come on back!

00:07:07.734 --> 00:07:10.467
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

